# (build 183) The music's fade-out writes one track too far (FadeOutMusic,
# ps2.asm:92206). It copies the chord's voice -- FM3's algorithm and four
# levels -- to as many tracks as the chord has parts, starting at the track
# after FM3's, so the last copy lands on the track past the chord: with
# every song's chord of three, the first effect track. An effect sounding
# there (on FM3) then works out its next volume steps from the music's
# voice, not its own.
#
# The game fades its music in three places, and only one has such an
# effect: Gaira's control panel, where the explosion starts 22 frames
# before the fade under Mystery. The explosion's FM3 part steps its volume
# down 8 every 8 frames, at frames 17, 25, 33, 41 and 49 of it; the fade
# arrives at frame 22. Its voice has three carriers, all at level 0, so a
# step writes its volume to $46, $4A and $4E (FM3's operators 3, 2 and 4).
#
# Mystery has two chord voices, the first for 1536 frames of its 2304 and
# the second for the other 768 (fade_out_overrun_second_chord). Under the
# first -- three carriers, levels $27, $12 and $04 -- the steps after the
# fade are those levels more: the explosion's end is quieter. Fails on 182,
# whose fade stopped at the chord's last part: every step wrote the
# explosion's own volume to all three registers.

start level $41 53 26        # Gaira, the cell below the control panel
wait screen level
wait idle
expect music $88             # Mystery
press up                     # the panel's wall
wait idle
wait ticks 1
expect object $37 visible
press a                      # the control panel
wait screen building
limit 2000
wait ticks 60
expect script $1901          # "Oh no! This satellite is headed straight for Palm!"
wait ticks 389               # 300 frames, the explosion, its step at frame 17
expect sound-register 1 $46 $08      # the explosion's own voice: volume 8
expect sound-register 1 $4A $08
expect sound-register 1 $4E $08
wait ticks 8                 # the fade at frame 22, the step at frame 25
expect sound-register 1 $46 $37      # volume $10 on the chord's levels,
expect sound-register 1 $4A $22      # $27, $12 and $04
expect sound-register 1 $4E $14
wait ticks 8                 # frame 33
expect sound-register 1 $46 $3F
expect sound-register 1 $4A $2A
expect sound-register 1 $4E $1C
wait ticks 8                 # frame 41
expect sound-register 1 $46 $47
expect sound-register 1 $4A $32
expect sound-register 1 $4E $24
